WEBVTT

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.290
I can't.

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:11.990
Will Sono and the others really come?

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.640
Yeah. It's Sono.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.990
Focus on digging.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.690
The trench?

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.820
It'll protect us from grenades.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.000
Let's go!

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.800
Attack!

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:37.800
Karira!

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.180
Don't be afraid!

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.430
Return fire!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.280
Ren! Kari!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.020
STELLA GIRLS' ACADEMY

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.020
HIGH SCHOOL DIVISION C  CLUB

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.520
I decided this myself

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.520
I decided that relying on chance

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:35.030
is just so ridiculously fruitless

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.990
I dwelled in my fantasies too much

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:45.910
I'm going to leave my safety zone behind

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.840
The future is opening up to me like a vast river

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.130
Even if sailing straight is difficult,

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:58.470
I will hold my head high

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.140
I'll change my life,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.180
and the gray rules that govern it

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:11.020
even if I trip and stumble on the way

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:16.940
Others are guiding me, but I will walk

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:23.660
My footprints in this world are so colorful

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.880
I'm serious!

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:44.890
The world around me transformed into a desert battlefield.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.950
There were tanks and
hundreds of soldiers!

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:50.400
You have to hit with arrows you don't have.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.070
No wonder we lost, then.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.260
Our garrison consisted only of us three.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.400
Hail our heroic sacrifice!

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.190
Am I weird?

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.740
Do you want more tea?

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.400
Yes, please.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:03.920
Me too!

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.740
I'm sure you saw what you saw.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.000
I believe you too.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.000
After all, I want to see it too!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.000
It sounds like so much fun!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.710
Thanks!

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:20.590
You've cheered up, Li'l Yura.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:24.210
All right then, let's declare you the winner for today.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.100
The winner is the one who has the most fun.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.190
So, if you have fun, you win?

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.110
Yeah.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.790
There are lots of ways to enjoy airsoft.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.710
It might look like we all play the same sport,

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.690
but everyone has different feelings about it.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.110
You've got your own idea of airsoft.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.660
My own idea of airsoft...

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.520
Yeah. Something only you can see.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.450
An idea that only you have.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.000
You enjoyed it, so you won.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.090
Well, you technically lost.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.040
Can it!

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.240
I'd like to get better and technically win, though.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.740
I see.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.410
Are you free now?

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.690
Sure.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.710
Then I'll train you!

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.100
Oh, I know what's coming.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.770
Oh yeah.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.520
How 'bout it?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.980
Of course!

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.980
One more... would be nice.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.030
Paper!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.490
Scissors.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.290
Sorry I'm late!

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.330
I've got something for you, Yura.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.180
I looked all over for it.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.210
This is...

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.710
A Škorpion vz. 61.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.440
It's a famous submachine gun from Czechoslovakia.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.670
Grab that part and pull it back.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.060
It's like the tail of a scorpion.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.220
Hence, Škorpion.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.740
Press firmly here.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:56.910
Yup, yup.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.380
It's small, but it packs a scorpion's poison.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.570
It's a good gun.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.070
Take care of it.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.330
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.040
I'm just lending it to you.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.180
Really?

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.700
I got this from my own teacher.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.790
I'll give you something even better!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.350
If you pass, that is.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.520
Wait!

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.550
Just a little more!

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.520
Yachiyo and Rento had no trouble with this.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.650
We went through her training last year.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.280
There's the goal.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.200
What is it?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.820
A fox! Look, a white fox!

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:01.340
It's gone.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:09.070
There might be an Inari shrine here, but that's pushing it, Yura.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:12.150
Did you "see" something again?

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:15.190
No, I think I was imagining it.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:21.810
There are other spirits besides Inari enshrined here, away from the public eye.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:28.400
One of them was a warrior from the Taira clan, enshrined here in the twelfth century.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.570
We're ready!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:32.810
Merci!

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.910
We don't know his name, though.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:42.710
According to legend, he was a brilliant, handsome young man, and was peerless with a bow since his teens.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.040
Nasu-no-Yoichi, maybe?

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.830
Well, he was a Minamoto, so maybe Taira-no-Yoichi?

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:51.590
I said nobody knows his name.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.060
Why is that?

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.490
Beats me.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:07:00.190
He died young in the chaos of the Genpei war.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:04.580
Would you want to talk to him if he appeared to you, Yura?

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.530
I guess so.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.670
I could at least ask him his name.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.070
Yura, you shouldn't wish for that,

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.260
or else the spirits might steal you away!

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:17.200
Th-That's not funny!

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:21.440
He probably died too early to have a girlfriend.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.980
Those are usually the most powerful spirits.

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.230
Take care not to get stolen away.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.600
Let's start, Yura!

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.670
O-Okay!

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:34.640
I shall now instruct you in airsoft, the art of Japanese gunfighting!

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.760
My gratitude!

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:39.940
What?

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.480
I'm supposed to hit that?

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.500
Aye.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.990
But it's super small!

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:48.520
And probably out of range, too.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.560
Look.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.120
Huh?!

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.190
It hit.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:06.390
This isn't so hard.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.700
Want to try too, Ren?

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:14.670
Can you hit it too, Ren?

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:16.970
Well, we'll see.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.680
It hit.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.030
The spirits helped me.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.960
I'm sure you can do it, too.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:32.310
Really?

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:34.480
I told you it wasn't hard.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.500
True.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.520
Grab your shoes.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:38.330
We're gonna try it from up close.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:41.830
Can you do it from here?

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:43.580
I think so.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.270
Why?

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:49.090
Why, why?

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.790
Yura, we're not doing target practice here.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:55.050
This is about understanding airsoft.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:00.300
Airsoft and aiming don't have anything to do with each other.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.350
Why do you think that is?

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.390
I don't know.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.370
Airsoft isn't that simple.

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:11.800
There's a lot of people in the fray, and the situation is always changing.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:15.700
The distance to your enemy, the distance to your comrades.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.440
Your own position.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:20.880
That's why having a straight barrel and nice backspin on the pellets doesn't matter.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.660
There's no way to hit through aim alone.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.110
So, what should you do to hit someone?

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:33.130
Um... get into point blank range before firing?

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:33.830
Yup.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.810
You can hit them once you see the fear in their eyes.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:41.350
To that end, you can think of shooting and being shot as the same thing.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:42.640
Do you know why?

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.170
Because you make yourself a target when you fire.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.790
Think of comrades, enemies,

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:54.110
and everything else on the skirm site as one and the same.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.820
Then you and the target will be...

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.070
zero meters away.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.620
Don't worry, Yura!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.150
I have no idea what she's saying either!

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:07.960
Sorry.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:12.690
My teacher... well, the one who taught me airsoft said it.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:16.380
I didn't understand what he was talking about either, at first.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.470
You'll understand it in time.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.950
Let's try again, Yura.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:21.970
You got it!

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.050
Look at the target now.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:25.950
Right.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:27.730
Don't aim, look!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.980
We'll now aim without aiming.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.210
Aim without aiming...

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:33.760
Yes.

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:35.480
And we will wait without shooting.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.720
This is called "shooting without shooting."

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.310
Shooting without shooting.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:42.080
Look. And wait.

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:44.970
Wait until the target comes to you.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:45.750
Okay.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.250
Until it comes.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.630
You fail because you seek success.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.600
To achieve success, you need to see everything as one.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.760
The pellet will hit if you become one with the world.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.340
Don't worry.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.680
Wait until it wants to be hit.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:06.540
There!

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.270
It hit!

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:11.320
Wow!

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:12.370
That was quick!

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:12.960
Yeah!

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.480
I'm really happy!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.630
All right, let's go back three steps and do it again.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:19.200
Three steps.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.270
You already got the hang of it?

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:24.280
Huh?

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:29.030
You see, that was already 99% of what I wanted to teach you.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.210
If you slowly increase the distance,

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.660
hitting it from where we started will seem like a piece of cake.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.170
You're so amazing, Yura!

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.220
This took us days to get the hang of!

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.340
We'll finish early at this rate.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.740
Want to go eat cake somewhere?

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:44.630
Are you treating me?

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.430
Don't lose focus.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:58.930
Again.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:00.490
Okay.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.240
That's weird.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.870
Sono, it's getting late.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:11.430
I see...

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:12.240
Okay then—

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.250
I'm not done.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.890
We promised we'd go home before the sun went down.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.940
We'll try again next time.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.690
On second thought, I'll buy you cake.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.500
Eating in the halls, huh?

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:29.980
What are you gonna do if your boobs get even bigger?

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.030
Good point.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:35.280
I guess I'll take only one sugar cube later.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.240
That's not what I meant...

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:40.860
Oh, your gun, Sono...

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.240
That can wait!

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.830
Don't take it out on a train.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:46.620
Is something wrong?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.830
Oh no, it's gone!

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.770
It must still be in the store.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.160
I didn't open my bag there!

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.140
It's probably at the shrine.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.420
I'm quite sure you put it in your bag back then.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:02.830
Sometimes, I space out and...

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:08.510
I'm going back!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.470
But now's—

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:10.470
I'll give you a call!

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.260
You have returned.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.260
You are Yura, correct?

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.120
How do you know my name?

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.450
Choujirou.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:43.050
Excuse me?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.410
That is my name.

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:50.050
You said you would ask me my name, did you not?

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:55.660
What is this, another weird delusion?

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:56.810
Weird delusion?

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:04.590
My once glorious family may have perished,
but is that not a bit rude?

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.650
Besides, I am a spirit!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.760
Sorry, Choujirou.

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:11.160
I have to look for something important now.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.430
See you around.

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.130
What do you think I am?

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:17.280
A figment of my imagination, right?

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:19.980
I must really be tired.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:21.070
You are wrong.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:25.250
Men are still connected to my divine realm.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:27.090
Divine realm, huh...

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.050
Fine.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:33.310
Yura,

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.100
I shall teach you true strength.

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.600
That is why I called you here.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:45.440
Let us begin.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:49.070
We shall go to your world and have you recreate mine.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.430
Where are we?

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.080
I told you.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.420
This is your own world.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.640
My realm and your world are resonating.

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.530
This is the age I lived in.

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.640
This is the last day of my life.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.290
The moment of my death.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:25.900
I fight forevermore.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:28.280
I fight a battle I cannot win.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.510
Time and time again.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.200
Will you lose?

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.530
Yes.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:38.120
I will lose and die.

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:40.540
There must be a way!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.540
Will you help me, then?

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:43.920
Am I able to?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.000
Yes.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.300
You must fire.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.410
But it's an airgun.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:55.510
Look closely. It's not a toy.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:02.470
You know that this world will be as you desire it.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.560
When you run away from reality,

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:09.070
you build a world where all is possible.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.820
This world has existed for you for as long as you can remember.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.820
Don't tell me that creepy stuff!

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:20.330
Yours is a great power that can assimilate the world.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:26.250
You do not flee into a dream, but rather turn the world into one!

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.250
The entire world is your home.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.050
I have no idea what you're talking about!

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:35.860
I thought you could rescue me.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:41.250
This is the end.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:56.160
Good to see you!

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.600
I was a bit worried.

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:00.660
I'm sorry I didn't answer the phone.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:02.910
It was at the shrine.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.620
Hey there, Choujirou.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.620
What did you just say?

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:10.800
Choujirou? My teacher called the gun that.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.350
Isn't it so exotic?

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:14.510
What's wrong, Yura?

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:16.780
Hey, Yura!

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.390
High School Division   Twelfth Grade   Kashima Sonora

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.390
High School Division    Tenth Grade      Yamato Yura

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:23.830
So that young warrior called himself Choujirou, huh?

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:24.790
Yes.

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:28.910
That's pretty crazy.

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:33.670
Sono, I...

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:37.230
What should I...

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:43.660
If you want to find the answer, let's go there tomorrow.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:48.740
You should decide whether you want to leave him to his fate or kill his enemies.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:56.590
My teacher was an American soldier.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:18:01.170
His unit was famous, and he fought on the front lines.

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:02.200
I see.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.790
And one day...

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.340
I got a call saying he was killed in action.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:12.480
Yeah, you can guess I wasn't too crazy about airsoft for a while.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:15.990
Of course.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.830
It didn't last forever, though.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:23.190
I realized that airsoft, too, means shooting others with guns.

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:25.990
So I took it up again.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.140
But why?

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:30.190
That's weird! It's wrong!

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:35.430
Didn't you say yourself that the winner is the one who has the most fun?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:37.720
So you lose if you don't have fun, right?

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:39.720
I guess.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:42.220
Aren't you losing, then?

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.060
Don't do that!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.790
I think I followed that up with something.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.040
It might look like we all play the same sport,

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:55.400
but everyone has their own idea of it.

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:59.000
I have my own idea of airsoft.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.450
I enjoy it from the bottom of my heart.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.910
I won't hear any complaints.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:06.540
Okay.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:11.310
If you find you can't enjoy airsoft after what's happened,

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:13.840
you can stop. It's fine.

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:30.560
Didn't she seem a bit off to you?

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.140
Will she be okay?

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:33.900
She'll be fine.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:39.400
She went to face a world only she can see.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:41.270
She'll be fine alone.

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:45.200
More pellets!

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.310
What on Earth...

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.610
Yura?

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:26.840
Yours is a great power that can assimilate the world.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:32.260
You do not flee into a dream, but rather turn the world into one!

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:36.660
The entire world is your home.

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:43.340
If this is my idea of airsoft...

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.490
I'm serious!

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:15.050
The world around me transformed into a medieval battlefield!

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:17.740
So, what'd Choujirou say?

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:20.580
"You have my praise!"

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:26.380
Seriously though, I had no idea you were into old geezers.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.670
Huh? Choujirou was young and super handsome.

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:33.160
Too bad the Minamoto slew him in his prime...

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:37.930
Didn't he survive and fight until he had a long white beard and all?

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:38.750
Huh?

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:42.170
Your own world is nice and all,

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:44.690
but you should get your history right.

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:46.690
Huh?

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:51.160
Oh yeah, here's a memento for your outstanding success.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:52.630
Choujirou!

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:54.200
But I couldn't—

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:57.020
You can have it if you love it so much.

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:58.080
Thanks!

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.300
Tea time!

00:21:59.300 --> 00:22:00.590
We have Darjeeling today.

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:03.710
It's the first second flush of the year!

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.050
Command!

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:12.930
Control!

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:15.180
Communication!

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:16.230
The C3 Club!

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:16.850
Yay!

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:20.060
Survival doesn't make the gunshots stop

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:23.400
Carrying the flag I hear gunfire

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:28.530
Smile, 'cause isn't this fun?

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:30.620
Yay!

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:36.750
I blush when I make eye contact with my comrade,

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.580
but that's fine

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:41.710
Let's trust each other and laugh

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:42.710
Ready?

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:45.210
3, 2, 1, go! Go!

00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:48.260
Take your comrade and get the flag!

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:51.970
Can't you feel your heart thump when you advance?

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:55.060
Let's hit them and laugh

00:22:55.060 --> 00:22:55.970
All right?

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:58.600
3, 2, 1, go! Go!

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.940
It can be hard, it can be vexing,

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.770
but when you overcome that

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:11.870
you'll smile like you never did before

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:13.580
Everyone, take up positions!

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:14.120
Okay!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:18.580
Survival doesn't make the gunshots stop

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:21.710
Carrying the flag I hear gunfire

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:25.800
Enjoy your youth, even if your tears are stolen

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:31.840
Telepathy, a step forward

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.890
Don't look down, look ahead

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:35.760
Sorry it took me so long to be enthusiastic about it!

00:23:39.810 --> 00:24:09.630
Preview

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:43.220
What's wrong, Hono?

00:23:43.220 --> 00:23:46.150
It's nothing big...

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:48.020
Let me give you advice!

00:23:48.020 --> 00:23:49.270
Me too! Me too!

00:23:49.270 --> 00:23:52.680
I'll solve anything for you that can be solved with money!

00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:55.320
You see, I think my bra size increased again,

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:57.560
so I can't wear the swimsuit I bought last year...

00:23:57.560 --> 00:23:58.500
Okay guys, go home.

00:23:58.500 --> 00:23:59.870
Gotcha.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:01.160
Hey!

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:09.630
Bask on an isolated island
to rise like a burning phoenix.

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:02.100
Next time.

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:03.600
Bask on an island to rise like a burning phoenix.

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:06.500
I don't think it's a problem if it spills out of your swimsuit.

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:08.070
And more every year.
